  "query_preview": "..\n\nKey Message 1)\n\nThe cold front which exited southeast of the area on Friday is over \nthe southeast CONUS and will eventually sink further south to the \nGulf Coast early in the new week. A deepening low pressure system \npassing well to our north will send another cold front southeast \nthrough the area Sunday evening. However, the first front well to \nthe south will keep the moisture supply cut off, and Sunday night's \nfront will come through dry. A modest drop in temperatures will \nfollow for a couple of days as surface high pressure builds in from \nthe northwest behind the front. This high departs to the east by \nmidweek and allows for returning south to southwest winds to carry in\nsomewhat warmer air. Another cold front may arrive late in the week \nunder persistent west northwest upper level flow. However, \nsignificant moisture will still be cut off near the Gulf Coast, and \nno rain is forecast.",
